.TH QCOM-BASEBAND-PROFILE-MANAGER 1 "September 2026" "0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qcom-baseband-profile-manager \- select resident Qualcomm modem profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qcom-baseband-profile-manager
.BI \-d " device"
.RB [ \-v | \-q ]
.RB [ \-c " config" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
An experimental OpenIMSd daemon that reads the primary provisioning SIM's
carrier identity and selects an appropriate modem-resident software profile
using QMI PDC. Profiles must already be loaded into the modem.
.PP
The program does not scan vendor partitions, upload MBN files, provision
embedded SIM profiles, or establish IMS bearers. Selecting a profile can
interrupt modem service. Do not run multiple carrier-policy owners together.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " URI"
Required QMI device, for example qrtr://0 or /dev/cdc-wdm0.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " FILE"
TOML configuration file. The CLI default is pdc.toml in the current directory.
The packaged service explicitly uses /etc/qcom-baseband-profile-manager.toml.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Reduce logging. Repeat to suppress additional log levels.
Cannot be combined with verbose mode.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qcom-baseband-profile-manager.toml
Administrator-supplied carrier-to-profile configuration for the service.
The package does not create this file or choose carrier IDs automatically.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/qcom-baseband-profile-manager/config.example.toml
An intentionally empty example with no carrier or fallback policy.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only the primary SIM is supported. Automatic catalogue import, coordinated
modem-restart recovery, and robust end-to-end error handling remain unfinished.
PocketFed images include this tool but preset its service disabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qmicli (1),
.BR ModemManager (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
